It's a design pattern where an object maintains a list of dependents (called observers).
and automatically notifies dependents/observers when there is a change in state.

Example:- Weather Station - where multiple devices receive updates from a weather station.
Social Media feeds - when we follow someone on instagram, we become observer of their profile. When they post new content, we are automatically notified.

There are 2 models:-
1. Push Model-  Observable pushes the data it want observer to receive
2. Pull Model- Observer holds observable object reference and when it got to know something updated, it pulls the data whatever it needs using Observable object.

Subject / Observable
- stores observers
- lets observers subscribe/unsubscribe
- notifies observers when something changes

Observer
- defines an update method
- reacts when notified

Push vs Pull Model
Model	Meaning	Advantage	Disadvantage
Push	Subject sends data to observer	Simple and direct	May send unnecessary data
Pull	Subject sends reference, observer fetches data	Flexible	Observer becomes dependent on subject interface